# Line endings are declared here, not left to each machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# Why it matters for THIS repo: the backend and frontend run inside Linux images (`backend/Dockerfile`
# does `COPY . .`, and the Makefile/`backend/scripts/init_db.sh` execute there). With core.autocrlf=true
# — the default on the Windows box this was prepared on — git rewrites those files to CRLF at checkout,
# and a CRLF shell script inside a Linux container fails with `bash\r: No such file or directory`.
# `eol=lf` wins over core.autocrlf on every platform, so a checkout anywhere is byte-identical here.
#
# The campaign's census records the EOL class of every file, and this is what keeps it LF-pure.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch, never normalise.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.zip binary

# Generated lockfiles are text and stay LF like everything else.
package-lock.json text eol=lf
